      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "despite their claims my world was removed from public and I was never given a reason or even an email stating as such and I most certainly didn't remove it myself\n\nThere is nothing against VRChats terms of service in it and it's fairly well optimized. and according to the website my world only ever got one report which was a while ago and I fail to see what in my world was even reportable so I doubt that was the cause\n\nNow I won't pretend that my world was super popular anyting but it had its fans and so it was very distressing to find that suddenly the people who enjoyed my world were no longer able to visit it and I had never been informed of this happening or why it was happening\n\nMy world has been public since before Labs was even a thing and I update it frequently",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-31T23:13:34.905Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As you probably know by now, there have been instances of worlds being removed from public unintentionally, as in https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/public-world-put-back-into-community-labs-after-update\n\nThere have also been cases of worlds which were, apparently, removed by vrchat staff without notifying the creator. This has led to instances where the creator republished, thinking that the issue was the above linked bug, and got a public ban as a result.\n\nOne such example is here: https://twitter.com/legaC_vr/status/1133395099684089856?s=19\n\nIn this Japanese Twitter thread, the uploader of \"Just Kongyo\" explains that, because of the above mentioned bug, the lack of any community labs suspension (which https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/submitting-a-world-to-be-made-public claims will happen if community guidelines are broken), and there not being a significant number of reports, he decided the removal was probably the result of the bug and re-labs'd the world, after which point he got a public ban.\n\nI don't intend to question your decision regarding whether the content of this world was appropriate; however, please review your processes for removing worlds and ensure that world creators are unambiguously notified when their worlds are removed, and told - at least in general terms - why the removal took place, to avoid this sort of confusion.",
